{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Hardcoded Add-On Data.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Hardcoded Add-On Data.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"hardcoded add on data hardcoded add on data","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Hardcoded Add-On Data.md","fileName":"Hardcoded Add-On Data.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Hardcoded Add-On Data","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 09:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Add-On Development Workflow]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Add-On Development Workflow","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Hardcoded Add-On Data.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Hardcoded Add-On Data.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"hardcoded add on data hardcoded add on data","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Hardcoded Add-On Data.md","fileName":"Hardcoded Add-On Data.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Hardcoded Add-On Data","heading":"Hardcoded Add-On Data","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Hardcoded add-on data stores vertices, faces, and related values directly in Python collections, then passes them into a new Blender mesh. This can tightly integrate a geometric template with the transformations and subsets an algorithm applies to it.\n\nThe same coupling is the method's weakness. Large numeric arrays clutter source code, are difficult for artists to replace, and can usually be read from an external interchange file instead. Hardcoding is most defensible when the data is small or inseparable from the algorithm, not merely because it avoids shipping another file.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Add-On Development Workflow","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Hardcoded Add-On Data.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/H